# Monorepo development — frontend & backend

**Stay with one repo** (`frontend/` + `backend/` + root docs). Do not split into separate repos.

Never commit feature work directly on `main`. Scope every change to the correct area on its own branch.

## Option A — Feature branch (single checkout)

```bash
git fetch origin
git checkout main && git pull origin main
git checkout -b feat/your-feature-name
```

Switch branches when changing focus. One feature per branch; one focused PR per branch.

## Option B — Git worktree (parallel frontend + backend)

Use when backend and frontend need to run **at the same time** in separate folders:

```bash
# From main clone
git fetch origin
git worktree add ../AiLanguageTutor-frontend feat/your-frontend-branch
git worktree add ../AiLanguageTutor-backend feat/your-backend-branch
```

Example:

```bash
git worktree add ../AiLanguageTutor-frontend feat/ui-mvp
git worktree add ../AiLanguageTutor-backend feat/openai-realtime-pr3-session-endpoint
```

Run backend in one folder (`uvicorn main:app --reload --port 8000`) and frontend in the other (`npm run dev`). Both share the same remote and history.

## Agent checklist before editing

1. Confirm current branch/worktree matches the task (frontend vs backend).
2. If changes are on the wrong branch, stop and move to a dedicated branch or worktree.
3. Do not mix unrelated frontend and backend changes in one PR.
4. Rebase or merge latest `main` before opening a PR if `main` has moved.

## Naming conventions

- Frontend UI: `feat/ui-*`
- Backend API: `feat/openai-realtime-pr*` or `feat/backend-*`

See `docs/dev-workflow.md` for full details.
